    "created_at": "2022-04-05T16:38:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-05T16:38:17Z",
    "body": "One can be supportive of declarative model of shadow DOM or custom elements, and still not supportive of the currently proposed form of declarative shadow DOM. Those are not contradictory positions.\r\n\r\nAs far as I've read it, the [following comment](https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/892#issuecomment-1079552552) is a false dichotomy and mischaracterization of Mozilla's view as I understand it.\r\n\r\n> That’s despite [recent blog posts](https://webvision.mozilla.org/full/) that seem to have a different view:\r\n> \r\n> > We also continue to see room for improving or adding primitives that provide declarative alternatives for situations that currently require JavaScript, such as…\r\n",
